## Final Judgement
The key insights from the fact-check are that uniformed Miami police officer Daniel Ubeda was photographed at an early voting site in Miami, Florida, wearing a "Trump 2020" mask. The Miami Police Department and Chief Jorge Colina publicly stated the behavior was unacceptable and a violation of departmental policy, and that it was being addressed immediately. Mayor Francis Suarez also confirmed the officer would be disciplined. Multiple credible news outlets reported the incident and the impending disciplinary action on October 20, 2020, the same date as the claim. No evidence contradicts that disciplinary action was initiated, though the exact form of discipline was not yet specified. The evidence clearly supports the claim.

